This solution iterates over the matrix row by row and column by column, and maintains the current line length for each position in the matrix. If the element is 1, it increments the current line length, and if the element is 0, it resets the current line length to 0. Also, it only considers the cells in the matrix that are either below or to the right of the current cell to avoid double counting. Therefore, it is an efficient solution for a large matrix.

